PREGUNTAS COMPLETAS:

Booking:
Q: How do I book an appointment?
A: You can book online at poppypawsgrooming.com/book, call us at (512) 677-0703,
or send us a message on Instagram @poppypawsgrooming. New clients always welcome!

Q: Do I need to be home during the appointment?
A: Someone should be available at the start and end of the appointment,
but you don't need to stay outside the whole time. We'll let you know when we're done.

Q: How far in advance should I book?
A: We recommend booking 1–2 weeks in advance, especially for first appointments
and weekend slots. For urgent grooming needs, call us — we'll do our best to
accommodate you.

Q: What is your cancellation policy?
A: We ask for at least 24 hours notice for cancellations or rescheduling.
We understand things come up — just give us a call.

Pricing:
Q: How much does mobile grooming cost?
A: Prices start at $105 for a Bath & Mini Groom and from $125 for a Full Groom.
Final price depends on your dog's size and coat type. We always provide a
clear quote before starting — no hidden fees, ever.

Q: Why does grooming cost more for doodles and double-coat breeds?
A: Doodles and double-coat breeds (Huskies, Aussies, Goldens) require specialized
techniques, more time, and specific products to groom properly and safely.
The additional cost reflects the extra care your dog's coat deserves.

Q: Is there a travel fee?
A: No travel fees within our standard service area (Williamson & Travis County).
Contact us if you're outside the area to discuss options.

Services:
Q: How does mobile dog grooming work?
A: We bring a fully-equipped Poppy Paws grooming van directly to your home or
preferred location. Your dog gets a private, one-on-one appointment — no cages,
no other dogs, no waiting. We handle everything; you just open the door.

Q: How long does a grooming appointment take?
A: Most appointments run 1.5–3 hours depending on your dog's size, coat type,
and the service. We never rush — your dog gets all the time they need.

Q: My dog gets really anxious. Is mobile grooming better?
A: Yes — for most anxious dogs, mobile grooming is significantly less stressful.
No other dogs, no kennel smells, no loud salon. Your dog gets our full, calm
attention in a familiar setting.

Q: What products do you use?
A: We use premium, pet-safe products. If your dog has known allergies or skin
sensitivities, please let us know when booking and we'll accommodate accordingly.

Q: Do you groom cats or other pets?
A: Currently, we specialize exclusively in dog grooming to ensure the highest
quality experience for every canine client.

Q: What is the anesthesia-free dental cleaning?
A: It's a gentle cosmetic teeth cleaning performed while your dog is awake.
We remove surface plaque and tartar without any sedation. This service does
not replace veterinary dental care, but is a great way to maintain your dog's
oral health between vet visits.

Areas:
Q: What areas do you serve?
A: We serve Georgetown, Austin, Round Rock, Cedar Park, Pflugerville, Leander,
Liberty Hill, Hutto, and surrounding Williamson & Travis County communities.
Not sure if we cover you? Call us at (512) 677-0703.

Q: Do you come to apartments or condos?
A: Absolutely! Our van is fully self-contained and doesn't require water or
electricity from your home. We can service any residential location with
adequate parking for our van.
